WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.935
Day one is a check, not a lesson.

2
00:00:02.385 --> 00:00:09.880
Two things look the same from the outside. Reading that is still hard work. And reading that is easy, but does not sink in.

3
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:16.619
This check tells them apart. You hold the grown-up page. Your child gets the page with the big words.

4
00:00:17.069 --> 00:00:18.247
There are three parts.

5
00:00:18.697 --> 00:00:25.175
Part A. Your child reads eight words. Mark a word only if it is read right, with no sounding out loud.

6
00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:32.144
Part B. Your child reads one sentence out loud. Then you ask the question printed beside it on your page.

7
00:00:32.594 --> 00:00:34.678
For example, your child reads this.

8
00:00:35.078 --> 00:00:36.391
The hen sat on a log.

9
00:00:36.891 --> 00:00:38.803
And you ask: Where did the hen sit?

10
00:00:39.603 --> 00:00:44.825
Part C is two short stories. Your child reads the first one. Cover it with your hand.

11
00:00:45.275 --> 00:00:50.161
Then say: tell me what happened. Mark each part your child tells you. Do not ask more.

12
00:00:50.611 --> 00:00:56.607
Then you read the second story aloud. It is printed on your page. Ask again: tell me what happened.

13
00:00:57.057 --> 00:01:01.537
That one shows whether your child follows a story when the reading is taken away.

14
00:01:01.987 --> 00:01:05.659
Do not teach, and do not correct today. Just listen and mark.

15
00:01:06.109 --> 00:01:11.826
Then read the yellow box at the bottom of your page, from the top. Stop at the first line that fits.

16
00:01:12.276 --> 00:01:19.547
One line is for the child whose reading is still hard work. That child needs a different plan first, and the page names it.

17
00:01:19.997 --> 00:01:28.000
One line is for the child who did not follow the story you read aloud. Then talk and read aloud every day, and tell the teacher.

18
00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:31.885
The other lines tell you which days of this plan to do twice.

19
00:01:32.335 --> 00:01:37.013
Write the three numbers on the page, and keep it. You will look at it again on the last day.
